                <head>No. 400<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On April 16, President Eisenhower delivered the address about which he had
                    consulted with Churchill, Mayer, and Adenauer. For the text of the address, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents of the United
                        States: Dwight D. Eisenhower, 1953</hi>, pages 179–188, or Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 27, 1953, pages 599–603.
                    Reaction to the speech as reported from the various United States posts abroad
                    is in file 611.00.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
